## Features of Computer Virus

## 1. Automatic Restart
Some viruses force the computer to restart automatically. This helps the virus activate during system boot and makes it harder for users to remove it.

## 2. System Heating
Viruses often run continuously in the background and use high CPU and memory. This increases system workload and can cause the laptop or PC to heat up more than usual.

## 3. Slow Performance
A virus consumes system resources like RAM, CPU, and storage. Because of this, the computer becomes slow, applications take longer to open, and overall performance drops.

## 4. File Replication
One major feature of a virus is self-replication. It creates copies of itself and spreads into other files, folders, USB drives, and sometimes across networks.

## 5. Hiding Automatically
Viruses are designed to stay hidden. They may disguise themselves as system files or run in the background so the user does not easily detect them.

## 6. Memory Usage
Many viruses stay active in system memory (RAM). They keep running silently and reload every time the computer starts, making them persistent.

## 7. Unauthorized Activities
A virus can perform actions without the user’s permission, such as opening unknown programs, showing pop-ups, changing settings, or downloading harmful files.

## 8. Data Damage or Theft
Some viruses delete files, corrupt data, or steal sensitive information like passwords and personal data.

---

# 📌 Conclusion
A computer virus is a harmful program that spreads, hides itself, slows down system performance, and may damage or steal data while using system resources without the user’s knowledge.
